    "attributes": {
        "action": "Adopt the \"citizen advance\": 28-40s may take \u00a312,500 advance & delay retirement",
        "additional_details": "The current cost-of-living and housing crises make it incredibly difficult for young adults to secure home deposits, clear high-interest debt, or invest in career training.A recent report by the Social Market Foundation think tank proposed a \"Citizens' Advance.\" This policy would allow working adults aged 28\u201340 with at least 10 years of National Insurance contributions to access a tax-free lump sum of roughly \u00a312,500 today. We urge the government to formally consider and debate this policy.",
        "background": "We call on the government to adopt the Social Market Foundation proposal allowing 28-to-40-year-olds to take a \u00a312,500 advance in exchange for delaying retirement by one full year.",
